$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: aReaction conditions: To a mixture of ligand I
(X mol %) and Nd(OTf)3 (20 mol %), which was stirred at 50 °C for 2 h and
then cooled to -25 °C, were added
(Z)-trimethyl(1-phenylprop-1-enyloxy)silane (48.8μmol, 1.5 equiv) and
benzaldehyde (32.5μmol, 1.0 equiv).
(syn)-3-Hydroxy-2-methyl-1-phenyl-3-(thiophen-2-yl)-propan-1-one (3d).
Yield 6.6 mg, 82%.The configuration of the product was determined as syn
by comparison with the 1H NMR spectra of authentic compounds.22 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3 , δ ) 7.96-7.93 (m, 2H), 7.62-7.58 (m, 1H), 7.51-7.46 (m,
2H), 7.25- 7.22 (m, 1H), 7.00-6.96 (m, 2H), 5.49 (t,J= 3.2 Hz, 1H),
3.84-3.76 (m, 1H), 3.59 (d,J= 3.2 Hz, 1H), 1.32 (d,J= 7.2 Hz, 3H); 13C
NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3 , δ ) 205.2, 146.0, 135.7, 133.9 (CH), 129.0 (CH),
128.7 (CH), 126.9 (CH), 124.5 (CH), 123.7 (CH), 70.7 (CH), 47.9 (CH),
12.3 (CH3); TLC Rf = 0.20 (8:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate); HRESIMS (m/z) [M +
Na]+ calcd for C14H14O2SNa, 269.0612; found, 269.0615; HPLC (Chiralpak
AD-H, isocratic 98.5:1.5 n-heptane/2-propanol,flow rate 0.8 mL/min, λ =
254 nm) 94:6 er; >99:1 syn:anti; tR= 56.87 min (major,syn), 71.46 min
(minor,syn)
