$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1S, 2S)-2-(2-Methoxy-ethoxymethoxy)-1-phenyl-but-3-en-1-ol (4b): A
suspension of 1 (0.73 g, 5 mmol) in THF (10 mL) was cooled to -78°C and
sec-BuLi (1.3 M in Hexanes, 3.66 mL, 4.76 mmol) was added dropwise. The
resultant bright yellow mixture was stirred at -78°C for 30 minutes. A
solution of (+)-B-methoxydiisopinocampheylborane (1.90 g, 6 mmol) in THF
(5 mL) was then introduced dropwise via cannula. After stirring 60 min at
-78°C, boron trifluoride etherate (0.95 mL, 7.5 mmol) was added, followed
by a pre-cooled (-78°C) solution of Benzaldehyde (530 mg, 5 mmol) in THF
(5 mL) via cannula. Stirring was continued at -78°C for 3 h, the reaction
mixture was oxidized via addition of 3 M NaOH (2.34 mL) and 30% H2O2
(2.38 mL). The biphasic solution was stirred for 8 h at ambient
temperature. The layers were separated, and the aqueous solution was
washed with Et2O (2×10 mL). The combined organic solutions were washed
with brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Flash
chromatography, using a gradient of ethyl acetate-hexanes as eluant gave
0.84 g (70%) of the homoallylic alcohol 4b. (1S,
2S)-2-(2-Methoxy-ethoxymethoxy)-1-phenyl-but-3-en-1-ol (4b), 0.84 g (70%)
yield 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 7.25 - 7.40 (m, 5H), 5.54 - 5.66
(m, 1H), 5.12 - 5.18 (m, 2H), 4.82 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 4.75 (d, J = 7.0
Hz, 1H), 4.59 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 4.19 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 3.58 - 3.70
(m, 2H), 3.49 (t, J = 4.5 Hz, 2H), 3.40 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3)
δ (ppm): 140.4, 134.3, 128.1, 127.7, 127.1, 119.2, 93.3, 82.2, 76.6,
71.8, 67.4, 59.0; EI-MS: m/z 195, 146, 120, 107, 89 [(CH2OCH2CH2OCH3)+,
100%], 77, 59; CI-MS: m/z 253 (M + H), 235 ((M + H) - H2O), 205, 147,
129, 89 [(C7H5)+, 100%]; HRMS-CI: (M + H) 253.1430 (actual), 253.1440
(calcd.); 95% ee based on HPLC (The alcohol was derivatized as its
p-nitrobenzoyl ester and analyzed on the HPLC and the ee was determined
to be 95%).
