$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-((Z)-2-Phenylethynyl-1-cyclooctenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (6a); Following the
General Procedure E; General Procedure E. To a stirred solution of 11
(4.50 mmol) in Et2O (25 ml) was added allyl Grignard reagent (0.81 M
solution in Et2O, 9.00 mmol) at 0 °C and stirred for 30 min. The mixture
was then quenched by addition of saturated aq. NH4Cl, extracted with
EtOAc three times, and washed with brine. The organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by silica gel column chromatography to give 6.
1,4-Bis(1-hydroxy-3-butenyl)-2,5-bisphenylethynylbenzene (6l); Following
the General Procedure E; Grignard reagent (4 equiv) was used.; The crude
product was dissolved in CHCl3 and purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 3/1) (Diastereomeric mixture: 91% yield,
white solid);. The following data are for a mixture of two diastereomers
(0.5/0.5); 1H NMR (CDCl3) 2.22 (d, J= 3.7 Hz, 1.0H), 2.23 (d, J= 4.0 Hz,
1.0H), 2.46-2.54 (m, 2.0H), 2.71-2.80 (m, 2.0H), 5.19-5.29 (m, 6.0H),
5.87-5.94 (m, 2.0H), 7.36-7.39 (m, 6.0H), 7.51 (m, 4.0H), 7.72 (s, 1.0H),
7.73 (s, 1.0H); 13C NMR (DMSO-d6) δ 42.78, 69.79, 69.90, 87.23, 87.29,
95.37, 95.42, 116.89, 119.66, 119.73, 122.15, 128.92, 129.10, 131.29,
135.34, 135.53, 146.04; HRMS (FAB) calcd for C30H26O2 (M+) 418.1933,
found 418.1932.
