$DATUM (6Z)-(4R*,5S*)-5-Hydroxy-8-(4-methoxybenzyloxy)-4,6-dimethyl-6-octen-3-one
((Z)-66). To a -78 °C solution of c-Hex2BCl (460 μL, 2.10 mmol) in Et2O
(3 mL) was added Et3N (319 μL, 2.29 mmol), followed by a solution of
3-pentanone (200 μL, 1.90 mmol) in Et2O (2 mL). After stirring at -78 °C
for 1 h, a solution of 65 (357 mg, 1.62 mmol) in Et2O (2 mL) was added.
The mixture was stirred for 1 h at -78 °C and placed in the freezer for
16 h. The reaction mixture was then partitioned between Et2O and a 1.0 M
aqueous NaH2PO4/NaOH buffer (pH ~ 7), the organic extract was
concentrated to give an oil which was taken up in MeOH (7.5 mL) and 1.0 M
aqueous NaH2PO4/NaOH buffer (pH ~ 7) (7.5 mL) was added and the solution
was stirred at 0 °C. H2O2 (2.5 mL, 30% solution in H2O) was then added
dropwise. After stirring at room temperature for 2 h, the mixture was
diluted with H2O and extracted with CH2Cl2 (2×). The combined organic
layers were washed with saturated aqueous Na2CO3, brine, dried over
MgSO4, and the solvent and cyclohexanol were evaporated under reduce
pressure and heating (~80 °C) to give the crude product which was
purified by flash chromatography using 40% Et2O/hexane to yield (Z)-66
(443 mg, 76%) as a colourless liquid. Rf = 0.14 (60% hexanes:ether);
(6Z)-(4R*,5S*)-5-Hydroxy-8-(4-methoxybenzyloxy)-4,6-dimethyl-6-octen-3-one
((Z)-66). yield 443 mg, 76% 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.26 (2H, m), 6.88
(2H, m), 5.60 (1H, m), 4.65 (1H, d, J = 9.5 Hz), 4.44 (2H, q, J = 11.4
Hz), 4.11 (1H, ddd, J = 11.7, 7.5, 0.9 Hz), 3.96 (1H, ddd, J = 11.7, 6.0,
1.1 Hz), 3.80 (3H, s), 2.77 (1H, app dq, J = 7.3, 2.5 Hz), 2.54 (2H, m),
2.31 (1H, br s), 1.74 (3H, d, J = 1.3 Hz), 1.06 (3H, t, J = 7.1 Hz), 0.89
(3H, d, J = 7.1 Hz); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 215.5, 159.2, 138.7,
130.1, 129.4, 126.2, 113.8, 72.2, 71.5, 65.2, 55.2, 48.7, 36.4, 17.5,
13.6, 7.5; IR (film) ν = 3426, 2972, 1712, 1613, 1514, 1454, 1302, 1248,
1174, 1035 cm-1; HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for ([M+Na]+) = 329.1734, found =
329.1723.
