$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (2S,3R)-4-(E)-methyl
3-hydroxy-2-methyl-5-phenylpent-4-enoate, 5a: 1H NMR (300
Trifluoromethanesulfonic acid (TfOH, 0.28 mL, 3.16 mmol) was added
dropwise at 0 °C to freshly prepared (-)-Ipc2BH3 (823 mg, 2.88 mmol)
suspended in CH2Cl2 (6 mL) and stirred for 1 h. The clear yellowish
solution of Ipc2BOTf [(-)-2] was cooled to -78 °C, and methyl propionate
(1a, 194 mg, 2.2 mmol) and triethylamine (0.66 mL, 4.8 mmol) were added
and stirred for 30 min. The mixture was then warmed to 0 °C and kept
stirring for 4 h when the enolate formation was complete as was shown by
the 11B NMR spectrum (shift from δ 61 ppm for (-)-2 to d 53 ppm for
enolate). The enolate was again cooled to -78 °C and the aldehyde 4 (2
mmol) was slowly added and stirred for 8 h. After completion of
aldolization, as determined by thin layer chromatography, pH 7 buffer
solution (5 mL) in 5 mL MeOH was added to the reaction mixture, followed
by the addition of 30% H2O2 solution (5 mL) in 5 mL MeOH and stirred for
5 h at RT. The reaction mixture then washed with water (10 mL), sat.
brine solution (5 mL) and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The combined
organic layers was concentrated in vacuo, the 1H NMR spectrum of the
crude product was plotted to determine the diastereomeric ratio, and was
purified via column chromatography (hexane: ethyl acetate = 95:5) to
provide syn-aldol product 5a-h in 63-85% yield. The enantiomeric ratio
was determined by the 1H and 19F NMR of the MTPA derivative (Mosher
ester) of the alcohols. General procedure for the preparation of
anti-aldol products: The above enolization reaction was performed at -78
°C for 3 h and aldolization was performed under similar conditions
replacing 1a and triethylamine with t-Butyl propionate (1e, 286 mg, 2.2
mmol) or isopropyl propionate (1d, 255 mg, 2.2 mmol) and
diisopropylethylamine (0.83 mL, 4.8 mmol), respectively.
(2S,3R)-4E-benzyl 3-hydroxy-2-methyl-5-phenylpent-4-enoate, 7a: 1H NMR
(300 Yield: 70%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): d (ppm) 7.28-7.14 (m, 5H), 6.60
(d, J = 15.9 Hz, 1H), 6.12 (dd, J = 6.0 Hz, J = 15.9 Hz, 1H), 5.12 (s,
2H), 4.55 (m, 1H), 2.73 (m 1H), 1.22 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3) d (ppm) 175.13, 136.55, 135.74, 131.75, 128.66, 128.33,
127.88, 126.64, 73.25, 66.65, 45.29, 11.74. HRMS-EI 296.1412 (calcd.),
296.1405 (actual). IR (cm-1) 3464, 2997, 2935, 1728, 1454.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, syn:anti=56:44, buffered solution (pH 7) used in stage
4, anti-aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Aldol Reaction with Diisopinocampheyl Enolborinates of
Propionates
