$DATUM Methyl 3-(4-fluorophenyl)-3-hydroxy-2-methylenepropanoate (18d).
Purification by column chromatography (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a
desired compound 18d (171 mg, 80%) as a colorless liquid. Spectral data
were identical to those previously reported.5 TLC: R f 0.48 (2:1
hexane/EtOAc). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.35 (dd, 2H, J = 8.8, 6.0 Hz),
7.03 (t, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 6.34 (s, 1H), 5.82 (s, 1H), 5.55 (d, 1H, J =
5.6 Hz), 3.74 (s, 3H), 2.99 (d, 1H, J = 5.6 Hz). 13C-NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 166.9, 162.6 (d, JCF = 244.3 Hz), 142.1, 137.2, 128.5 (d, JCF =
7.5 Hz), 126.3, 115.5 (d, JCF = 21.0 Hz), 72.9, 52.2. LRMS (FAB) m/z (rel
int): 193 ([M-OH]+, 91), 233 ([M+Na]+, 14).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium hexafluorophosphate
as solvent gave lower yield
