$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To an oven-dried vial were added molecular
sieves (3 Å ), tetrahydrosalen ligand (+)-5 (12 mg, 0.02 mmol, 10 mol%)
and (CuOTf)2.C6H5CH3 (1 mg, 0.002 mmol, 1 mol%). To this mixture was
added anhydrous MeOH (0.8 mL) followed by the nitroalkane (0.6 mL) and
the resulting green suspension was stirred at room temperature for 10
min. To the suspension at 40 °C was added the aldehyde (0.2 mmol) and the
mixture was stirred at that temperature for the length of time specified
in Tables 3 - 5. The reaction mixture was concentrated under reduced
pressure and the resulting crude residue was treated with aqueous HCl
(1M, 2 mL, 2 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) and was stirred at room temperature
until the green color had disappeared. (R)-1-(2-Furyl)-2-nitroethanol
(7l) pale yellow oil, yield 87%. 94% ee [Chiralcel OD, hexane:i-propanol
90:10, 1 mL/min, 215 nm, tR (major) 40.7 min, tR (minor) 45.9 min];
[α]25D- 40.9 (c 0.22, CH2Cl2), [lit.9 for (R) enantiomer [α]16D-33.2 (c
1.0, CH2Cl2, 95% ee)]; IR (neat) 3528, 3154, 2954, 2924, 1642, 1554,
1502, 1380, 1351, 1159, 1090, 1020, 966, 875, 805, 739, 691 cm-1; 1H NMR
(700 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.84 (s, 1H), 4.68 - 4.73 (m, 1H), 4.82 - 4.89 (m,
1H), 5.48 - 5.56 (m, 1H), 6.41 - 6.47 (m, 2H), 7.45 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (175
MHz, CDCl3) δ 64.7, 79.2, 109.1, 110.2, 142.8, 151.1.
