$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure for enantioselective Henry reaction
promoted by per-6-ABCD (1) Per-6-ABCD 1, (0.112 g, 0.1 mmol) was
suspended in ACN:Water (1:1, v/v) (3 mL). Aldehyde 2a-z (0.02 g, 0.1
mmol) dissolved in acetone (0.5 mL) was added dropwise to 1 with constant
stirring and continued for an hour to complete complexation. Then
nitromethane 3 (0.005 mL, 0.1 mmol) was added and allowed to stir at -20
°C for 7 h. After completion of the reaction, products were extracted
with ethyl acetate, dried with sodium sulphate and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The resulting crude product was purified by passing
over a column of siliga gel 60-120 mesh using petether/ ethyl acetate
(7/3 ratio as an eluent) affording Henry product 4a-z as a light
yellow-dark yellow viscous oil liquid which was analyzed by NMR
spectroscopy (300 MHz, CDCl3, T = 300 K, TMS = 0 ppm), ESI-MS and
CSP(Chiral Stationary Phase)-HPLC. Percentage ee was determined by HPLC
at 254 nm using chiralcel OD-H column, with n-hexane and i-propanol
mixtures at a flow rate 0.5-1.0 mL/min. (or it otherwise noted). After
extraction of the product, per-6-ABCD (1) is washed thrice with ethyl
acetate, filtered, dried in vacuum and reused.
1-(Furan-2-yl)-2-nitroethanol (Table 2, Entry 18): Compound 4r was
prepared according to the general procedure and purified by column
chromatography (pet-ether/ethyl acetate = 7/3) to give a yellow viscous
oil (99% yield). 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, δ ppm): 3.38 (br s, 1H), 4.38
(dd, J = 3.3, 13.5 Hz, 1H), 4.60 (dd, J = 9.0, 13.5 Hz, 1H), 5.22 (dd, J
= 9.0, 3.3 Hz, 1H ), 7.21 (t, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.52 (d, J = 9.2 Hz, 1H),
7.80 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H). 13C-NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, δ ppm): 71.5, 72.1,
84.2, 105.9, 143.3, 150.6. ESI-MS: m/z Calcd. for C6H7NO4 [M+H]+ :
158.0453; Found, 158.0468 (Rel. Int.100%). HPLC: Enantiomeric excess was
determined by HPLC with a Chiralcel OD-H column (85:15
n-hexane-isopropanol, 0.8 mL/min, 254 nm); major enantiomer tmajor = 58.7
min, minor enantiomer tminor = 64.7 min, 92% ee.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Henry Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Per-6-amino-β-cyclodextrin as a Reusable Promoter and Chiral Host for
Enantioselective Henry Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
