$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Method of 1,2-Addition of Nitromethane
to Aromatic Aldehydes. A mixture of 3 (37.7 mg, 0.050 mmol), nitromethane
(1.0 mL, 18.7 mmol), and benzaldehyde (101.9 μL, 1.0 mmol) was stirred
under a nitrogen atmosphere. After being stirred under room temperature
for 8 h, the solvent was removed. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel (chloroform) to afford the
corresponding 1,2-adduct. The spectral data of the obtained 1,2-adducts
were identical to previous results.31 Yield 86%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Henry reaction, nitromethane also used as solvent
