(S)-2-Nitro-1-phenylethanol ((S)-4a) 1-(Furan-2-yl)-2-nitroethanol (4h)
(S)-4h and (R)-4h Products were prepared using 2-furaldehyde (0.5 mmol,
41 μL) by General Procedure A and General Procedure B, respectively. The
crude product was purified by column chromatography with silica (20%
ethyl acetate in hexanes) to afford the title compound in 80% (S)-4h and
88% (R)-4h yields. (S)-4h 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz): δ7.41-7.42 (m, 1H),
6.36-6.41 (m, 2H), 5.47 (dd, 1H, J = 3.4, 9.3 Hz), 4.78 (dd, 1H, J = 9.3,
13.6 Hz), 4.67 (dd, 1H, J = 3.4, 13.6 Hz), 2.85 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 125 MHz,): δ150.7, 143.2, 110.6, 108.2, 78.3, 64.8. (8)
1-(furan-2-yl)-2-nitroethanol (4h): t1 = 22.11 min t2 = 23.84 min (AD-H
Column, hexanes/2-propanol : 95/5, 0.8 mL/min) or t1 = 55.10 min t2 =
60.10 min (AD-H Column, hexanes/2-propanol : 97/3, 0.5 mL/min)
