$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for the preparation of
chiral α-sulfinylenones Optically active (Rs, E)-1-alkenyl sulfoxide (1.0
eq) was treated with 0.5 M LDA / THF solution (1.1 eq) for 30 min at -78
°C. The α-lithiated carbanion was generated, and then aldehyde was
dropwise added to the carbanion solution at the same temperature and
stirred for 15 min. The mixture was quenched with sat. aq. NH4Cl
solution, extracted with EtOAc washed with sat. aq. NH4Cl solution
followed by brine. The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4 . Evaporation
and flush column chromatography on silica gel. The mixture used next step
without furthermore purification. Diastereomixture of α-sulfinylallylic
alcohol (1.04 g, 2.73 mmol; 91 % yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric synthesis of γ-hydroxy α-enones by
1,8-diazabicyclo[5.4.0]undec-7-ene-catalyzed stereoselective
rearrangement of chiral α-sulfinyl enones
