$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for Reformatsky reaction: synthesis of β-hydroxy esters
(13b-13h) (13a is commercially available) TMSCl (1.2 equiv) was added to
a suspension of Zn dust (1.6 equiv) in Et2O (0.4 M solution) at rt. The
resulting mixture was stirred for 15 min and then heated to reflux whilst
a mixture of aldehyde (1.0 equiv) and ethyl bromoacetate (1.2 equiv) was
added at such a rate so as to maintain a gentle reflux (~ 20 min). The
reaction mixture was heated at reflux for 1 h and then allowed to cool to
rt before quenching carefully with hydrochloric acid (2 M, 1 × volume of
organic phase). The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was
extracted with Et2O (2 × volumes of aqueous phase). The combined organic
extracts were washed with H2O (1/6 × volume of organic phase), brine (1/6
× volume of organic phase) and then dried (MgSO4). The volatiles were
removed under reduced pressure and the resulting β -hydroxy ester used
directly without further purification. Ethyl
3-furan-2-yl-3-hydroxy-propanoate (13b) See general experimental: a
mixture of 2-furaldehyde (2.00 mL, 24.0 mmol) and ethyl bromoacetate
(3.20 mL, 48.0 mmol) was added to a suspension of Zn dust (2.50 g, 38.4
mmol, activated with TMSCl (3.60 mL, 28.8 mmol)) in Et2O (60 mL). Aqueous
work-up afforded alcohol 13b as a brown oil (3.94 g, 89%, purity 85% by
1H NMR) which was used without any further purification in the following
step: Data were consistent with those reported in the literature.3 Rf =
0.29 (20% EtOAc in hexane); νmax(film)/cm-1 3442br s (OH), 3145m, 3120m,
2979s, 2937s, 2905m, 1726s (C=O), 1632w, 1504m, 1465m, 1445s, 1399s,
1373s, 1348s, 1281s,1252s, 1156s, 1035s, 1001s, 949m, 925m, 883m, 854s,
812m, 746s, 702m, 684m; δH (300 MHz) 1.27 (t, J 7.0, 3H, OCH2CH3), 2.82
(dd, J 16.5, 4.4, 1H, CHaHbCO2Et), 2.92 (dd, J 16.5, 8.5, 1H,
CHaHbCO2Et), 3.12 (br s, 1H, OH), 4.18 (q, J 7.0, 2H, OCH2CH3), 5.13 (dd,
J 8.5, 4.4, 1H, CHOH), 6.26 (d, J 3.3, 1H, =CH), 6.33 (dd, J 3.3, 1.8,
1H, OCH=CH), 7.37 (d, J 1.8, 1H, OCH=CH); δH (75 MHz) 14.1 (CH3,
OCH2CH3), 39.8 (CH2, CH2CO2Et), 60.9 (CH2, OCH2CH3), 64.2 (CH, CHOH),
106.2 (CH, =CH), 110.2 (CH, =CH), 142.1 (CH, OCH=), 154.7 (quat. C,
furan), 171.9 (quat. C, C=O); m/z (EI) 184 ([M]+, 4%), 166 (37,
[M-H2O]+), 121 (100, [furylCH=CHCHO]+), 97 (50), 65 (50), 39 (72), 138
(25, [furylCH=CHCO2H]+).
