$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
1-Trimethylsilyl-2-methyl-1-propenylmagnesiumbromide. A flask was charged
with Mg turnings (1.2 equiv) and THF (1 M) under nitrogen. Neat
1,2-dibromoethane (0.1 equiv) was added and the mixture was stirred at rt
for 5 min. Neat 1-bromo-2-methyl-1-trimethylsilylpropene8 (1.0 equiv) was
added in one portion, and the suspension was stirred at rt for 5 h. A
portion of the resulting Grignard reagent was then titrated against
menthol in the presence of 1,10-phenanthroline as an indicator.9 General
procedure for addition of
1-Trimethylsilyl-2-methyl-1-propenylmagnesiumbromide to aldehydes. A
solution of 1-trimethylsilyl-2-methyl-1-propenylmagnesiumbromide (1.5
equiv) in THF (~0.5 M) was slowly added to a solution of the desired
aldehyde (1.0 equiv) in THF at -78 °C. The reaction was stirred at -78 °C
for 15 min, then quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (equal volume to
solvent), warmed to rt and extracted with ether (3 × 30 mL). The combined
organic extracts were dried over sodium sulfate, filtered, and
concentrated. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography on
silica gel using 1% ethyl acetate/hexanes as the eluant.
(1R,2R)-1-[2-Vinyl-2-(triethylsiloxy)cycloheptyl]-4-methyl-3-(trimethylsilyl)pent-3-en-2-ol
(27a). Reaction of 0.22 mmol of 20a following the general procedure
afforded 81 mg (87 %) of the title compound as a colorless oil. This
material was judged to be a 2:1 mixture of diastereomers by NMR analysis.
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.97 (dd, J = 10.8, 17.3 Hz, 0.5 H), 5.89 (dd,
J = 10.8, 17.3 Hz, 1 H), 5.20-4.95 (m, 3 H), 4.68-4.65 (m, 1 H),
4.61-4.57 (m, 0.5 H), 2.04-1.92 (m, 1.5 H), 1.90-1.20 (m, 28.5 H),
0.96-0.90 (m, 13.5 H), 0.63-0.55 (m, 9 H), 0.21 (s, 9 H), 0.18 (s, 4.5
H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 145.6, 145.4, 143.8, 142.3, 138.1, 137.3,
111.8, 111.4, 8.09, 80.8, 73.7, 72.7, 46.1, 44.9, 41.55, 41.47, 38.9,
38.3, 30.45, 30.41, 29.7, 27.9, 27.4, 25.9, 25.8, 22.5, 22.4, 22.1, 21.7,
7.3, 7.2, 7.12, 7.09, 2.53, 2.47; IR (film) 3486 cm-1. Anal. calcd for
