$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B: To a stirred solution of
the exocyclic enol ether (1.20 mmol) and the carbonyl derivative (1.00
mmol) in 1.5 mL THF was added zinc(II)chloride (0.5 mL of a 0.4 M
solution in THF, 0.2 mmol) dropwise. After the time specified in Table 2,
the reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the residue purified
directly by flash column chromatography. Dihydropyran 20: The reaction of
2-methylenetetrahydropyran (1), and 2,3-butanedione (9) was conducted
according to the general procedure B. The crude residue was purified by
flash chromatography (SiO2; CH2Cl2:ethyl acetate, 10:1 → 2:1; with 5%
triethylamine). Dihydropyran 26: The reaction of
2-methylenetetrahydropyran (1), and (E)-4-benzyloxy-2-butenal (15)4 was
conducted according to the general procedure B. The crude residue was
purified by flash chromatography (SiO2; hexanes:ethyl acetate, 8:1 → 2:1;
with 5% triethylamine). Dihydropyran 26 (76%) as a yellow oil. TLC: R f =
0.39 (hexanes:EtOAc, 2:1). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 7.32 (5H, m), 5.81
(2H, m), 4.60 (1H, t, J = 3.7 Hz), 4.53 (2H, s), 4.34 (1H, m), 4.04 (2H,
d, J = 5.0 Hz), 4.00 (2H, m), 2.52 (1H, br s), 2.30 (1H, dd, J = 14.2,
3.3 Hz), 2.17 (1H, dd, J = 14.2, 8.4 Hz), 2.02 (2H, m), 1.80 (2H, m). 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 151.2, 138.3, 135.0, 128.3 (2C), 127.7 (2C),
127.5, 126.8, 98.6, 72.0, 70.1 (2C), 66.2, 42.3, 22.2, 20.1. IR (film):
3225, 3062, 2999, 2835, 1677 cm-1. HRMS (ESI) Calcd for C17H22O3
([M+Na]+): 297.1461, found: 297.1456.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
