$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the bromoallylboration
of aldehydes. (R)-5-Bromo-1-phenyl-hex-5-en-3-ol (18a): To a flame dried
25 mL round bottom flask equipped with a rice-needle stir bar is added
47.0 mg (0.10 mmol, 10 mol%) of R,Rdiol 4b and 16.1 mg (0.152 mmol, 0.15
equiv) of anhydrous Na2CO3, and 50 mg of 4Amolecular sieves (previously
dried under high vacuum at 100 °C and stored in oven). The flask is
capped with rubber septum and put under argon followed by the addition of
1.0 mL of freshly distilled toluene. The mixture is stirred for 2 min
followed by addition of 76 μL of 1.0 M CH2Cl2 solution of SnCl4 (0.076
mmol, 0.076 equiv)). Thus obtained mixture is stirred at room temperature
for 5 min and cooled to -78 °C and maintained at this temperature for 15
min. This is followed by addition of 280 mg (1.10 mmol) of
bromoallylboronic acid pinacol ester 1d. This mixture is then stirred for
additional 30 min after which, 132 μL (1.00 mmol) of hydrocinnamaldehyde
is added to the reaction mixture. The reaction is allowed to stir for 24
h at to -78 °C after which, 2.0 mL of 1.0 M toluene solution of DIBAL-H
is added to quench unreacted aldehyde. The reaction mixture is allowed
stir for additional 15 min at -78 °C after which 4 mL of 1N HCl. The
reaction mixture is then allowed to warm to room temperature and allowed
to stir for 30 min. Thus obtained mixture is extracted with 3 x 15 mL of
Et2O, and the combined organic extract is washed with brine (15 mL) and
dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated under vacuo to
give an oily residue, which is purified by flash chromatography (5% EtOAc
/ hexanes) to provide 151 mg of the requisite homoallylic alcohol product
18a in 86% yield with spectral properties identical to literature.
(R)-1-(3,5-Bis-trifluoromethyl-phenyl)-3-bromo-but-3-en-1-ol (18d):
Following general procedure for the preparation of 18a, the title
compound was obtained in 94 % yield. The enantiomeric excess was
determined to be 94.5% ee by derivatization with (S)-Mosher acid
chloride. [α]D 25 +6.78 (c 0.18, CHCl3); IR (cast film) 3425, 2944, 1719,
1632, 1376, 1279, 1174, 1135, 897, 708; 1H NMR (500 MHz,CDCl3) δ 7.87 (s,
2H), 7.82 (s, 1H), 5.72-5.73 (m, 1H), 5.61 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.17-5.20
(m, 1H), 2.77-2.85 (m, 2H), 2.45 (d, J = 2.5 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (125.69
MHz, CDCl3) δ 145.2, 131.8 (q, J = 33.3 Hz), 128.6, 126.0, 123.2 (q, J =
272.4 Hz), 121.7 (m), 121.2, 70.4, 51.5. HRMS-EI (m/z ): [M-C3H4Br]+
calcd for C9H3F6O 241.00880; found, 241.00877.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (96% ee), molecular sieves used (4A)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rationally Improved Chiral Bronsted Acid for Catalytic Enantioselective
Allylboration of Aldehydes with an Expanded Reagent Scope
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Rauniyar, Vivek; Hall, Dennis G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(11), 4236-4241

