$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Organolithium Addition General Procedure : 17
(2.5 equiv) in Et2O (0.5M) was added dropwise to a solution of t-BuLi (5
equiv, 1.7 M in pentane) at -78 °C. The solution was allowed to stir for
2.5 hours at -78 °C before slowly adding a solution of the carbonyl
compound (1 equiv) in Et2O or THF (1M - 0.1M, depending on solubility).
The dry ice/acetone bath was removed immediately and the solution was
allowed to warm to room temperature over 30 minutes. The solution was
quenched with aqueous saturated NH4Cl and extracted with Et2O. The
organic extracts were washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography (hexanes: diethyl ether). 12i. Yield 90%. 1H NMR (600 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 9.18(s, 1H), 7.77(d, J= 8.6 Hz, 1H), 7.68(d, J= 8.9 Hz, 1H),
7.66(d, J= 8.6 Hz, 1H), 7.46(t, J= 8.6 Hz, 1H), 7.32(t, J= 8.6 Hz, 1H),
7.12(d, J= 8.9 Hz, 1H), 5.73(dd, J= 8.9, 3.9 Hz, 1H), 4.73(s, 1H),
4.69(s, 1H), 2.87(s, 1H), 2.09(t, J= 7.8 Hz, 1H), 2.03(m, 1H),
1.88-1.75(m, 2H), 1.72(s, 3H), 1.64(m, 1H). 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3): δ
154.3(C), 145.6(C), 131.3(C), 129.7(CH), 129.1(CH), 128.9(C), 126.8(CH),
123.1(CH), 121.1(CH), 120.0(CH), 117.9(C), 110.5(CH2), 72.7(CH),
37.6(CH2), 26.1(CH2), 23.9(CH2), 22.5(CH3). HRMS (ESI) m/z calculated for
C17H20O2: 256.1463. Found 279.1354 (M + Na). IR (neat) cm-1 : 3383, 3329,
3071, 2936, 1624, 1601, 1466, 1404, 1265, 1227, 887, 814.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternatively reaction carried out using tetrahydrofuran as solvent in
stage 2
