$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 3-(9H-fluoren-9-ylidene)-2,2-dimethyl-1-phenylpropan-2-ol
(37). To a stirred solution of aldehyde 3 (1.46 g, 6 mmol) in anhydrous
Et2O (50 mL), phenyllithium (5.5 mL, 1.6 M in cyclohexane/Et2O) was added
dropwise and under an argon atmosphere. The reaction mixture was refluxed
for 1 h and warmed to room temperature. The mixture was poured into
ice-water and extracted with Et2O. The combined organic layers were dried
(MgSO4), filtered and concentrated to dryness. Flash chromatography using
hexane/ Et2O (99:1) afforded 37 (1.90 g, 97%) as a yellow oil. 1H NMR
(200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.08-8.04 (m, 1H, Ar), 7.72-7.56 (m, 3H, Ar),
7.38-7.18 (m, 9H, Ar), 6.96 (s, 1H, CH═C), 5.10 (d, J= 2.8, 1H, CHOH),
2.02 (d, J= 2.9, 1H, OH), 1.45 (s, 3H, CH3), 1.36 (s, 3H, CH3); 13C NMR
(50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 141.9 (C), 141.2 (C), 140.8 (C), 138.3 (CH), 138.1 (C),
135.8 (C), 135.2 (C), 128.6 (CH), 128.3 (CH), 128.1 (CH), 127.9 (CH),
127.8 (CH), 127.7 (CH), 127.5 (CH), 127.2 (CH), 127.0 (CH), 126.8 (CH),
119.7 (CH), 119.6 (CH), 119.0 (CH), 80.2 (CH), 41.4 (C), 24.4 (CH3), 22.8
(CH3); IR (neat) % 3421, 1601 cm-1 ; Anal. (C24H22O).
