$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Asymmetric Reaction
of 1,4- cyclohexadienyltributyltin (4) (GP1). A 10 mL Schlenk tube was
charged with a stirring bar and flushed with Ar. (S)-BINAP (6.3 mg, 0.01
mmol, 10 mol%), AgOTf (2.6 mg, 0.01 mmol, 10 mol%) and toluene (0.20 mL)
were added. The mixture was stirred under Ar at room temperature for 10
minutes. After cooling to -50 °C, a solution of an aldehyde (0.10 mmol,
100 mol%) in toluene (0.20 mL) was added followed by dropwise addition of
cyclohexadiene 1 (75 mg, 0.20 mmol, 200 mol%). After being stirred for 40
h at -50 °C, the mixture was diluted with pentane. The resulting
suspension was purified by flash chromatography over silica gel to afford
the corresponding homoallylic alcohol (9:1, pentane:MTBE). The
enantiomeric ratio and the absolute configuration were determined after
aromatization using DDQ (GP2).
(S)-Cyclohexa-2,5-dien-1-yl-(2-methylphenyl)methanol (5j; R = 4-MeC6H4)
Homoallylic alcohol 5j (R = 2-MeC6H4) was obtained using 2-MeC6H4CHO (12
mg, 0.10 mmol) by applying GP1 in 84% yield as a colorless oil. [α]25 D
-160° (c 0.84, CHCl3). IR (neat) 3420 (brs), 3026 (s), 2860 (m), 2819
(m), 1489 (m), 1460 (m), 1422 (w), 1042 (m), 945 (m), 852 (w), 760 (m),
741 (s), 689 (s) cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 7.47 (d, J = 7.7 Hz,
1H; Ar-H), 7.25-7.20 (m, 1H; Ar-H), 7.19-7.12 (m, 2H; Ar-H), 5.98-5.88
(m, 2H; vinyl-H), 5.67-5.54 (m, 2H; vinyl-H), 4.90 (d, J = 4.7 Hz, 1H;
CHOH), 3.18-3.06 (m, 1H), 2.77-2.66 (m, 2H), 2.33 (s, 3H), 1.94 (brs, 1H;
CH-OH) ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 140.3 (s), 134.4 (s), 130.3 (d),
127.6 (d), 127.5 (d), 127.1 (d), 126.3 (d), 126.1 (d), 125.9 (d), 123.9
(d), 73.2 (d), 41.7 (d), 26.6 (t), 19.2 (q) ppm. MS (ESI): 223 ([M +
Na]+). HRMS: ([M + Na]+) C14H16ONa: 223.1093; found: 223.1101.
