$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-[α-Phenyl-α-hydroxymethyl]thiophene (8). The condensation of
2-lithiothiophene with benzaldehyde (3.2 g, 3.2 mL, 30.418 mmol) followed
by column chromatography on silica using petroleum ether/ethyl acetate
(95:5) gave 8 as white solid (3.8 g, 77% yield). M. P. 53-55 °C. IR (KBr
film, cm-1) 3250 (OH). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, δ in ppm) 2.45 (br s, 1H),
6.05 (s, 1H), 6.88 (m, 1H), 6.92 (m, 1H), 7.27 (m, 1H) 7.36 (m, 3H), 7.44
(m, 2H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 72.3, 124.8, 125.4, 126.4, 126.8,
129.3, 137.8, 140.4, 148.5. ESMS: C11H10SO, calcd av mass 190.3, obsd m/z
191.0 (M+, 10%), 173.0 (M+-17, 90%). Anal. calcd: C, 69.44; H, 5.30; S,
16.85. Found: C, 69.38; H, 5.19; S, 16.83.
