$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for the Preparation of (2E,4E)-4-Carbinol Dienoates:
Synthesis of 2a. p-Chlorobenzaldehyde (70.4 mg, 0.5 mmol) was dissolved
in 1.0 mL of TBAF (1 M in THF, 2 equiv, 1 mmol). The mixture was stirred
in an ice bath for 3 min before compound 1a was added dropwise. The
reddish solution was stirred for 2 h. Then, saturated NH4Cl solution (10
mL) was used to quench the reaction. After being stirred for 5 min at
room temperature, the mixture was extracted with ether (2 x 20 mL). The
organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and the filtrate was concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by flash silica gel column chromatography
(9:1, 8:1, 6:1, 4:1, 2:1 hexanes: ethyl acetate) to give 2a (119.4 mg,
0.35 mmol, 70%) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 0.90 (3H,
t, J = 7.0 Hz), 1.26 (3H, t, J = 7.0 Hz), 1.31-1.34 (4H, m), 1.46 (2H,
m), 2.35 (2H, q, J = 7.5 Hz), 2.61 (1H, br s), 4.16 (2H, q, J = 7.0 Hz),
5.42 (1H, s), 5.85 (1H, d, J = 16.0 Hz), 6.14 (1H, t, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.29
(4H, m), 7.58 (1H, d, J = 16.0 Hz); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 14.2,
14.6, 22.7, 28.2, 29.4, 31.7, 60.7, 74.3, 119.8, 128.3, 128.3, 128.9,
128.9, 133.7, 136.3, 138.2, 140.8, 140.8, 167.5; MS (EI) m/z 336 (M+),
320, 291, 274, 263; IR (neat) ν 3435, 2956, 2857, 1709, 1691, 1489, 1282
cm-1. Anal. Calcd for C19H25ClO3: C, 67.75; H, 7.48. Found: C, 67.96; H,
7.44.
