$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (B) General Procedure for Asymmetric
Allylation of Aldehydes In a Schlenk tube, Pd(OAc)2 (1.5 mg, 6.7 μmol),
(R)-4 (5 mg, 14.1 μmol) and THF (0.8mL) were added under nitrogen. The
reaction mixture was stirred at 25 oC for 30 min, then the fresh
distilled benzaldehyde (18 mg, 1.7 mmol), cinnamyl alcohol (19 mg, 1.4
mmol) and Et3B (0.7 mL, 1.0 M in hexane, 0.7 mmol) were added
sequentially. After stirred at 25 oC for 12 hours, the consuming of
cinnamyl alcohol was complete monitored by TLC. The reaction mixture was
diluted with ethyl acetate (40 mL) and hydrolyzed with 3 M hydrochloric
acid (10 mL). After separated with aqueous phase, the organic layer was
washed with saturated aqueous NaHCO3, and brine, dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4 and concentrated in reduced pressure. The product was purified by
a flash chromatography with ethyl acetate/petroleum ether 1:6 to afford
anti-(1R,2S)-1,2-diphenylbut-3-en-1-ol 13a5 as a colorless oil.
anti-1-(2-Furyl)-2-phenylbut-3-en-1-ol (13g): colorless oil, 73% yield
78% ee. [α]15D +47 (c 0.19, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.32-7.13
(m, 6H, Ar-H), 6.28-6.16 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 6.01 (d, J = 3.0 Hz, 1H, CH),
5.30-5.23 (m, 2H, CH2), 4.89 (dd, J = 8.1 and 3.9 Hz, 1H, CH), 3.84 (t, J
= 8.1 Hz, 1H, CH), 2.27 (d, J = 3.9 Hz, 1H, OH); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 154.1, 141.9, 140.3, 137.6, 128.4, 128.1, 126.8, 118.6, 110.1, 107.6,
70.9, 55.9; MS (EI) m/z 214 (M+, 2), 39 (100); Anal. calcd for C14H14O2:
C 78.48, H 6.59; Found: C 78.29, H 6.62. HPLC (Chiralpak AD-H column,
n-Hexane/2-PrOH = 98:2, 0.9 mL/min) tR = 20.2 min (major), tR = 21.6 min
(minor).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, anti:syn = 99:1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Application of Chiral Spiro Phosphocin Ligand in
