$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: anti-(E)-Butyl
7-hydroxy-6,8-dimethyl-5-methylenenon-2-enoate (4a) According to the
general procedure A the catalyst was prepared from zinc iodide (32 mg,
0.10 mmol), zinc dust (7 mg, 0.10 mmol) and CoBr2(dppe) (31 mg, 0.05
mmol) in 0.5 mL dichloromethane. Then n-butyl acrylate (0.08 mL, 0.55
mmol) and isoprenylpinacolboronic ester 1 (107 mg, 0.55 mmol) were added
to the reaction mixture which subsequently was stirred for 16 h. After
dilution and cooling to 0 °C isobutyraldehyde (0.05 mL, 0.50 mmol) was
added and the reaction mixture was stirred at this temperature for 1 h.
After quenching with triethanolamine (0.08 mL, 0.55 mmol), work up and
purification by flash column chromatography (silica gel,
pentane/diethylether 2:1) the desired product 4a was obtained.The dr was
determined with the signals at 6.97 and 6.82 ppm. anti-(E)-Butyl
7-hydroxy-6-methyl-5-methylene-7-(thiophen-2-yl)hept-2-enoate (4i)
According to the general procedure A the catalyst was prepared from zinc
iodide (32 mg,0.10 mmol), zinc dust (7 mg, 0.10 mmol) and CoBr2(dppe) (31
mg, 0.05 mmol) in 0.5 mLdichloromethane. Then n-butyl acrylate (0.08 mL,
0.55 mmol) and isoprenylpinacolboronic ester 1 (107 mg, 0.55 mmol) were
added to the reaction mixture which subsequently was stirred for 16 h.
After dilution and cooling to 0 °C thiophen-2-carbaldehyde (0.05 mL, 0.50
mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred at this temperature
for 1 h. After quenching with triethanolamine (0.08 mL, 0.55 mmol), work
up and purification by flash column chromatography (silica gel,
pentane/diethyl ether 2:1) the desired product 4i was obtained. The dr
was determined with the signals at 5.88 and 5.70 ppm. A colorless oil
(152 mg, 0.49 mmol, 99%, dr 95:5). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ = 7.28-7.26
(m, 1H), 7.03-6.93 (m, 3H), 5.88 (dt, J = 15.6, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.10 (s,
1H), 4.99 (s, 1H), 4.77 (dd, J = 8.7, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 4.14 (t, J = 6.6 Hz,
2H), 2.95 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 2.61-2.51 (m, 1H), 2.35 (d, J = 3.0 Hz,
1H), 1.69-1.60 (m, 2H), 1.46-1.34 (m, 2H), 0.96-0.92 (m, 6H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ = 166.4, 148.1, 145.9, 126.4, 124.9, 124.8, 123.3,
114.1, 73.1, 64.2, 49.3, 36.5, 30.7, 19.2, 16.7, 13.7. IR (film, cm-1):
3471, 3077, 2961, 2934, 2874, 1718, 1653, 1458, 1386, 1311, 1278, 1213,
1163, 1066, 1028, 988, 905, 854, 834, 732, 700. MS (EI): m/z = 308 (M+,
2), 290 (22), 275 (2), 233 (9), 217 (11), 196 (41), 174 (19), 161(14),
149 (100), 134 (39), 113 (74), 95 (59), 79 (17), 68 (9), 57 (9). HRMS
(EI): calculated for C17H24O3S: m/z = 308.1446; found m/z = 308.1438.
