$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The asymmetric SE' allylation began with formation of the (S,S)-reagent 5
(R3 = Br) by the addition of BBr3 (0.22 mL, 1 M in CH2Cl2) into a
solution of anhydrous (R,R)-1,2-diamino-1,2-diphenylethane
bis-N,N-toluenesulfonamide (115 mg, 0.22 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.3 mL) at 0
°C. This mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 15 minutes, and then warmed to
room temperature and allowed to stir for 60 minutes. The solvent was
removed in vacuo and the resulting yellow solid was redissolved in dry
CH2Cl2 (2 mL) and allowed to stir for 10 minutes. The solvent was again
removed in vacuo and the resulting yellow solid was resuspended in dry
CH2Cl2 (2 mL). This sequence was usually repeated one or more times prior
to the introduction of 2-bromo-3-(tri-nbutylstannyl)-1-propene (110 mg,
0.275 mmol) and the mixture was then allowed to stir at room temperature
overnight (8-9 hrs). The reaction was then cooled to -78 °C, and a
solution of aldehyde 13 (42.1 mg, 0.16 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) was then
introduced into the cold solution. The reaction was stirred at -78 °C for
2 hours and was then quenched at that temperature by the dropwise
addition of aqueous pH 7 buffer (1 mL). The quenched reaction mixture was
allowed to warm to room temperature and a solution of saturated aqueous
NaHCO3 (5 mL) was added with additional stirring for 10 min. The phases
were separated and the aqueous phase was extracted three times with
CH2Cl2. The combined organic phases were dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was washed with hexanes and
filtered to remove the insoluble sulfonamide ligand. The solution of
hexanes was concentrated in vacuo to yield a crude material which was
purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc in hexanes,
1:2) affording the desired alcohol 23. 1H NMR analysis indicated that the
reaction stereoselectivity is 94:6 dr based on the integration of
selected proton signals. Yield 51.4 mg, 0.134 mmol, 84% (94:6). Rf = 0.54
(hexanes:EtOAc = 2:1); [α]D22 -30.3 (c 1.03, CHCl3); IR (thin film,
cm-1): 3439, 2959, 2931, 2856, 1631, 1612, 1513, 1462, 1302, 1248, 1172,
1093, 1034; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 7.23 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 2H),
6.87 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 2H), 5.66 (s, 1H), 5.48 (s, 1H), 5.00 (d, J = 8.0
Hz, 1H), 4.82 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H), 4.45 (d, A of AB, JAB = 12.0 Hz, 1H),
4.41 (d, B of AB, JAB = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 3.42 (dd, J = 8.0,
4.0 Hz, 1H), 3.10 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.80 - 2.67 (m, 3H), 2.58 (dd, J =
12.0, 4.0 Hz, 1H), 1.74 (s, 3H), 1.45 - 1.35 (m, 1H), 1.22 - 1.10 (m,
1H), 0.86 (dt, J = 8.0, 2.0 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm):
159.4, 138.4, 132.0, 130.9, 129.9, 129.5, 118.6, 113.9, 73.6, 73.0, 66.7,
55.3, 45.4, 39.6, 25.0, 18.0, 11.9; HRMS-ESI (calc. for C19H27O3Br [M]+)
382.1138, found 382.1147.
