$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B for ZnII-Catalyzed System
(R)-2-Nitro-1-phenylethanol ((R)-4a) 1-(Furan-2-yl)-2-nitropropan-1-ol
(5a, 6a) Products were prepared using 2-furaldehyde (0.5 mmol, 41 μL) and
nitroethane (5 mmol, 0.36 mL) by General Procedure A and General
Procedure B, respectively. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography with silica (20% ethyl acetate in hexanes) to afford the
title compound in 75% 5a and 85% 6a yields. 6a 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz):
syn product: δ7.41 (m, 1H), 6.39 (m, 1H), 6.34-6.37 (m. 1H), 5.04 (d, 1H,
J = 8.9 Hz), 4.94 (dt, 1H, J = 8.9, 6.9 Hz), 3.03 (br s, 1H), 1.36 (d,
3H, J = 6.9 Hz); anti product: δ7.37 (m, 1H), 6.34-6.37 (m, 2H), 5.31 (d,
1H, J = 4.1 Hz), 4.84 (dt, 1H, J = 4.1, 6.9 Hz), 3.08 (br s, 1H), 1.56
(d, 3H, J = 6.9 Hz); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz,): syn product δ 150.7,
143.3, 110.6, 109.4, 86.3, 69.4, 16.2; anti product δ51.2, 142.8, 110.5,
108.2, 84.9, 68.9, 13.1. (11) 1-(furan-2-yl)-2-nitropropan-1-ol (5a, 6a):
(AD-H Column, hexanes/2-propanol : 97/3, 0.5 mL/min); anti-6a: t1 = 51.14
min (major) t2 = 53.38 min (minor), syn-6a: t1 = 74.05 min (major) t2 =
80.95 min (minor)
