$DATUM General Procedure for the Preparation of β,β-Difluorinated Homoallylic
Alcohol Derivatives A vigorously stirred suspension of indium powder
(1.38 g, 12.0 mmol), aldehyde (10.0 mmol), DMF (20.0 mL) was cooled to
0°C in an ice bath, and 3-bromo-3,3-difluoropropene (1.88 g, 12.0 mmol)
was slowly added via a dropping funnel. After the addition was completed,
the reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature and stirring
was continued overnight. To work up, 10% aqueous hydrochloric acid (30.0
mL) was added to the reaction mixture, and excess indium were removed by
suction filtration and the residues were washed with ether (30.0 mL). The
organic layer was separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with
ether (2 x 50.0 mL). The combined organic extracts were washed with brine
(50.0 mL), then dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. The residues were purified by column
chromatography. The desired compound. methyl
4-(2,2-difluoro-1-hydroxybut-3-enyl)benzoate (1h’) Prepared from methyl
4-formylbenzoate using general procedure to afford 1h’ as a white solid
(2.06 g, 85%). (elution: 25% EtOAc/petrol; Rf = 0.3 w/ 50% EtOAc/petrol)
M.p.: 55-56°C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, 293 K, TMS): δ ppm 7.90 (d, J =
8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.49 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 5.93-5.76 (m, 1H), 5.58-5.44 (m,
2H), 4.97 (t, J = 9.3 Hz, 1H), 3.90 (s, 3H), 3.14 (br, 1H). 19F NMR (282
MHz, CDCl3): δ ppm -106.9 (AB, J AB = 247.3 Hz, 3 J HF = 9.0 Hz, 1F),
-109.4 (AB, J AB = 247.0 Hz, 3 J HF = 11.3 Hz, 1F). 13C NMR (100.7 MHz,
CDCl3, 293 K, TMS): δ ppm 167.0, 141.2, 130.3, 129.3, 129.0, 127.6, 121.9
(t, J = 9.4 Hz), 119.4 (t, J = 243.5 Hz), 54.4 (t, J = 30.6 Hz), 52.2. IR
(thin film): υmax 3467, 3003, 2955, 2898, 1779, 1614, 1578, 1438, 1419,
1287, 1114, 1073, 996, 957, 761, 747, 714 cm-1. Anal Calculated for
C12H12F2O3: C 59.50, H 4.99. Found: C 59.67, H 5.02.
