$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A. Alkyne Addition to
Unsaturated Aldehydes To an oven-dried round-bottomed flask under N2
atmosphere was added ZnBr2 (104 mg, 0.398 mmol). The flask was charged
with Et2O, then alkyne (2.0 mmol), diisopropylethylamine (700 μL, 519 mg,
4.01 mmol), aldehyde (4.0 mmol), and TMSOTf (432 μL, 530 mg, 2.39 mmol)
were added sequentially. The heterogeneous mixture was stirred for 1 h,
then passed through a filter of silica (1.0 cm x 3.0 cm) with Et2O. The
mixture was concentrated in vacuo, then dissolved in THF (6 mL). The
solution was stirred with 1.0 M HCl (3 mL) for 15 min, then diluted in
Et2O and washed with water (1x) and saturated NaHCO3 (1x). The organic
layer was diluted with hexanes (1:2 hexanes:Et2O) and dried over Na2SO4.
The solvent was removed in vacuo and the residue was purified by column
chromatography (5-20% EtOAc/hexanes). 1-(2-Furyl)-3-phenylprop-2-yn-1-ol
(4) The title compound5 was prepared according to General Procedure A,
using phenylacetylene (220 μL, 205 mg, 2.00 mmol) as the alkyne and
2-furaldehyde (332 μL, 385 mg, 4.01 mmol) as the aldehyde. The product
was isolated as an orange oil (89% yield): IR (film) 3355, 2917, 2233,
1483, 1441, 1219, 1134, 1002, 963, 909, 882, 808, 726 cm-1; 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.51 (dd, J = 1.5, 7.0 Hz, 2H), 7.48-7.46 (m, 1H),
7.40-7.33 (m, 3H), 6.56 (d, J = 3.3 Hz, 1H), 6.41 (dd, J = 1.9, 2.9 Hz,
1H), 5.72 (d, J = 5.5 Hz, 1H), 2.39 (d, J = 5.7 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3) δ 153.0, 143.1, 131.9, 128.8, 128.3, 122.1, 110.5, 107.9,
86.2, 85.8, 58.7; HRMS (ESI): Exact mass calcd for C26H20O4Na [2M+Na]+,
419.1254. Found 419.1249.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Trimethylsilyl Trifluoromethanesulfonate-Accelerated Addition of
Catalytically Generated Zinc Acetylides to Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Downey, C. Wade; Mahoney, Brian D.; Lipari, Vincent R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(7), 2904-2906

