$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Baylis-Hillman reaction: Enantioselective
Baylis-Hillman Reaction Employing 10. To a 10 mL round bottom flask,
flame dried and equipped with a stir bar, was added peptide 10 (0.0015
mmol), dissolved in CHCl3/THF (1:2, 0.5M), L-proline (0.0015 mmol),
aldehyde 1 (0.015 mmol), and methyl vinyl ketone (0.029 mmol). The
resulting mixture was stirred until complete loss of starting material
was observed by TLC (2:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate). The reaction was diluted
with chloroform and purification via flash chromatography (SiO2, CHCl3).
2.7 mg (81%) of 2 as a pale yellow oil.
3-[Hydroxy-(2-nitro-phenyl)-methyl]-but-3-en-2-one (2). 1 H NMR (CDCl3,
400 MHz) δ 7.98 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.78 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.66 (t, J
= 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.47 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 6.22 (s, 1H), 6.17 (s, 1H), 5.79
(s, 1H), 3.49 (bs, 1H), 2.37 (s, 3H); 13 C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 199.5,
149.0, 147.8, 136.7, 133.5, 128.8, 128.5, 126.6, 124.5, 67.1, 26.2; IR
(film, cm-1) 3414, 1675, 1525, 1351; TLC R f 0.52 (40% ethyl
acetate/hexanes); [α]D -114 (1.0, CHCl3, 78% ee); Exact mass calcd. for
[C11H11NO4 + Na]+ requires m/z 244.0586. Found 244.0585 (ESI+). Assay of
enantiomeric purity: Enantiomers of product were separated by chiral HPLC
employing a Chiralcel AD column (Diacel). Conditions: 95:5 hexanes:
2-propanol; Flow rate 0.75 mL/min; 29.8 min (minor ent), 32.5 min (major
ent).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Baylis-Hillman reaction, optimization study, optimized
on peptide catalyst length, highest stereoselectivity obsd. with an
8-residue peptide, enantiomer produced depends on isomer of proline used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Dual Catalyst Control in the Amino Acid-Peptide-Catalyzed
Enantioselective Baylis-Hillman Reaction
