$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(4-Hydroxy-4-phenylbut-2-ynyl)-acrylamide (2b). A solution of 0.511 g
(4.68 mmol) of 1b in 30 mL of THF was treated at -78 °C with 5.80 mL
(9.30 mmol) of a 1.6 M solution of n-BuLi in hexane, stirred for 15 min
at -78 °C, treated with a solution of 0.481 g (4.53 mmol) of benzaldehyde
in 1 mL of THF, warmed to 0 °C over 1 h, and stirred for 1 h. The
reaction mixture was quenched with 1.0 M HCl (40 mL) and extracted with
EtOAc (2 × 25 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine (40
mL), dried (MgSO4), concentrated under reduced pressure, and
chromatographed on SiO2 (65%-40% hexanes:EtOAc) to afford 0.697 g (71%)
of 2b as a colorless oil. Rf 0.15 (50% hexanes:EtOAc); IR (neat) 3313,
3066, 2924, 2243, 1655, 1542, 1451, 1248, 1133, 1004 cm-1; 1H NMR δ 7.52
(dd, 2 H, J= 7.8, 1.6 Hz), 7.43-7.32 (m, 3 H), 6.32 (dd, 1 H, J= 17.0,
1.3 Hz), 6.08 (dd, 1 H, J= 17.0, 10.3 Hz), 5.70 (br, 1 H), 5.69 (dd, 1 H,
J= 10.3, 1.2 Hz), 5.49 (br, 1 H), 4.25-4.23 (m, 2 H), 2.17 (br, 1 H); 13C
NMR δ 165.6, 140.4, 130.0, 128.6, 128.4, 127.4, 126.6, 83.5, 81.8, 64.3,
29.6; MS (EI) m/z (rel intensity) 215 (M+, 3), 214 (18), 198 (7), 197
(15), 169 (12), 168 (10), 144 (47), 143 (30), 131 (26), 116 (25), 115
(49), 105 (23); HRMS (EI) m/z calculated for C13H12NO2 (M-H) 214.0868,
found 214.0867.
