$DATUM 3-Hydroxy-4-methyl-7-(1-methyl-4-oxo-cyclopent-2-enyl)-hept-4-enoic acid
tert-butyl ester (14) To a stirred solution of t-butylbromoacetate (100
L, 0.68 mmol) in ether (1 mL) was added activated zinc (53 mg, 0.81
mmol). The mixture was refluxed for 2 h (until no more zinc was consumed)
then cooled to 0°C. This milky solution 0.7 M (450 L, 0.31 mmol) was then
added to the insaturated aldehyde 13 (50 mg, 0.26 mmol) in THF (2 mL) at
0 °C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 90 min, warmed to room
temperature and stirred for 16 h. The mixture was diluted with saturated
ammonium chloride solution. The mixture was decanted and the aqueous
phase was extracted with ether. The combined organic phases were washed
with brine, dried and concentrated under vacuum. The residual oil was
purified by flash-chromatography using ether-pentane (50 : 50) then ether
to yield the -hydroxyester 14 (37 mg, 46 %) (85 % corrected yield) as a
colorless oil along with the starting aldehyde (23 mg, 46 %). Molecular
formula: C18H28O4. IR (film, cm-1) : 3435, 1714, 1676. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3, ppm) : 7.40 (d, 1H, J = 5.6 Hz); 6.00 (d, 1H, J = 5.6 Hz); 5.38
(td, 1H, J = 1.1 Hz, J = 7.0 Hz); 4.31 (quint, 1H, J = 4.0 Hz); 3.09 (d,
1H, J = 3.4 Hz); 2.35-2.45 (m, 2H); 2.20 (dd (AB system), 2H, J = 18.6
Hz, J = 58.8 Hz); 1.81-2.00 (m, 2H); 1.56 (s, 3H); 1.45-1.61 (m, 2H);
1.42 (s, 9H); 1.26 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, ppm) : 209.8, 172.6,
172.0, 136.0, 131.9, 125.5, 125.5, 81.2, 73.2,73.1, 47.6, 44.9, 41.04,
39.9, 28.1, 26.2, 23.2, 12.0.MS (m/e) : 252 (M+-C4H8). HRMS: (M+-C4H8)
Calculated : 252.1361 ; found : 252.1357 ± 0.0007.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cascade Polycyclization: Exploration of a Convergent Route to Access
