$DATUM (R,E)-methyl
4-hydroxy-15-(5-((R,E)-11-hydroxy-14-methoxy-14-oxotetradeca-9-en-
1,12-diynyl)furan-2-yl)pentadeca-5-en-2,13-diynoate (10): A stock
solution of propiolate acetylide was prepared as follows: to a
flame-dried test tube under argon at room temperature was added toluene
(5 mL), dimethyl zinc (1.2 mL, 2.0 M solution in toluene, 2.4 mmol), and
methyl propiolate (.213 mL, 2.4 mmol). After 90 minutes, 2.6 mL of this
stock solution (0.975 mmol zinc acetylide, 6 equiv) was added to another
test tube containing dialdehyde 4 (64.7 mg, 0.165 mmol) and
(S,S)-bisprolinol ligand 1 (21 mg, 0.033 mmol). The reaction was sealed
and stirred at 4 °C for 3 days. After completion the reaction was
quenched with saturated aqueous ammonium chloride (3 mL), separated, and
the aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (3x10 mL). The organic layer
was concentrated and purified via silica gel chromatography (2:1 pet.
ether: ethyl acetate) to yield a clear/yellow oil (65 mg, 71%). Rf =
0.16, IR (thin film): 3410, 2930, 2856, 2236, 1718, 1578, 1518, 1435,
1254, 1193, 1093. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz): _ 6.39 (s, 2H), 5.92 (2H, dt,
J = 20, 9 Hz), 5.59 (2H, ddt, J = 20, 7.5, 1.5 Hz), 4.95 (2H, t, J = 1.5
Hz), 3.79 (s, 6H), 2.41 (4H, t, J = 9 Hz), 2.08 (6H, m), 1.27-1.63 (18H,
m). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 126 MHz): _ 153.8, 137.2, 135.6, 126.8, 114.5, 95.0,
86.3, 76.7, 70.9, 62.6, 52.9, 31.9, 28.6 (2 carbons), 28.5, 28.1, 19.4.
[α]D = -24.5° (c = 1.6, CHCl3).
