$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: anti-(E)-Butyl
7-hydroxy-6,8-dimethyl-5-methylenenon-2-enoate (4a) According to the
general procedure A the catalyst was prepared from zinc iodide (32 mg,
0.10 mmol), zinc dust (7 mg, 0.10 mmol) and CoBr2(dppe) (31 mg, 0.05
mmol) in 0.5 mL dichloromethane. Then n-butyl acrylate (0.08 mL, 0.55
mmol) and isoprenylpinacolboronic ester 1 (107 mg, 0.55 mmol) were added
to the reaction mixture which subsequently was stirred for 16 h. After
dilution and cooling to 0 °C isobutyraldehyde (0.05 mL, 0.50 mmol) was
added and the reaction mixture was stirred at this temperature for 1 h.
After quenching with triethanolamine (0.08 mL, 0.55 mmol), work up and
purification by flash column chromatography (silica gel,
pentane/diethylether 2:1) the desired product 4a was obtained.The dr was
determined with the signals at 6.97 and 6.82 ppm. anti-(E)-Butyl
7-hydroxy-7-(4-methoxyphenyl)-6-methyl-5-methylenehept-2-enoate (4 g)
According to the general procedure A the catalyst was prepared from zinc
iodide (32 mg, 0.10 mmol), zinc dust (7 mg, 0.10 mmol) and CoBr2(dppe)
(31 mg, 0.05 mmol) in 0.5 mL dichloromethane. Then n-butyl acrylate (0.08
mL, 0.55 mmol) and isoprenylpinacolboronic ester 1 (107 mg, 0.55 mmol)
were added to the reaction mixture which subsequently was stirred for 16
h. After dilution and cooling to 0 °C 4-methoxybenzaldehyde (0.06 mL,
0.50 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred at this
temperature for 1 h. After quenching with triethanolamine (0.08 mL, 0.55
mmol), work up and purification by flash column chromatography (silica
gel, pentane/diethyl ether 2:1) the desired product 4 g was obtained.The
dr was determined with the signals at 6.99 and 6.67 ppm. A colorless oil
(122 mg, 0.37 mmol, 74%, dr 90:10). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ =
7.28-7.23 (m, 2H), 6.99 (dt, J = 15.7, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 6.90-6.85 (m, 2H),
5.88 (dt, J = 15.6, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.10 (s, 1H), 4.98 (s, 1H), 4.42 (dd, J
= 8.9, 2.1 Hz, 1H), 4.14 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 2.95 (d, J =
7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.54-2.44 (m, 1H), 2.12 (s, 1H), 1-69-1.60 (m, 2H),
1.46-1.34 (m, 2H), 0.94 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H), 0.82 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H).
13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ = 166.4, 159.2, 148.6, 146.1, 134.6, 128.1,
127.9, 123.2, 113.9, 113.7, 76.7, 64.2, 55.3, 48.7, 36.5, 30.7, 30.6,
19.2, 16.7, 13.7. IR (film, cm-1): 3498, 3075, 2960, 2874, 2837, 1717,
1653, 1612, 1513, 1463, 1385, 1304, 1249, 1173, 1066, 1034, 988, 900,
834. HRMS (ESI): calculated for C20H28O4Na: m/z = 355.1880; found m/z =
355.1891.
