$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the addition of
metallated derivatives to aldehydes. To a stirred solution of amine 1
(307 mg, 1 mmol) in freshly distillated THF (10 mL) at -80°C, was added
dropwise 1.1 eq of sec-Buli 1.3M in hexane (846 μL, 1.1 mmol). The
mixture was then allowed to warm to -40°C over 30 min. In case of zinc or
copper derivatives, the lithium derivative was cooled to -80°C and 1.1 eq
of a molar solution of ZnBr2 or 1.2 eq of a dry mixture of CuCN/2LiCl in
dry THF (5ml) was added slowly. The mixture was stirred at -60°C for 15
minutes and then cooled to -80°C. A solution of aldehyde (1.1 eq in 3 mL
THF) was added dropwise. When the reaction was completed, the mixture was
hydrolysed with H2O or NH3/NH4Cl solution and diluted with ether. The
organic layer and the etheral extracts from the aqueous layer were
combined and washed with saturated sodium chloride solution, then with
water and dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. The solvent was
evaporated in vacuo and the products 5a-g were isolated by silica gel
chromatography purification (cyclohexane/ethyl acetate 98/2).
4-dibenzylamino-2,2-dimethylsilanyl-hex-5-yn-3-ol 5a anti
3-dibenzylamino-1-timethylsilanyl-hept-5-en-1-yn-4-ol 5f anti
3-dibenzylamino-1-timethylsilanyl-hept-5-en-1-yn-4-ol 5f syn Yield 83% in
88:12 ratio. anti : 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) 7.31 (m, 10H), 5.77 (dq, J =
6.4 Hz, J = 16 Hz, 1H), 5.49 (ddd, J = 6.6 Hz, J = 16 Hz, J = 1.48Hz,
1H), 4.15 (t, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 3.85 (d, J = 14 Hz, 2H), 3.49 (d, J = 8 Hz,
2H), 3.40 (d, J = 14 Hz, 2H), 1.76 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H), 0.24 (s,9H). 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 100MHz) 139.5, 131.5, 129.4, 128.7, 127.6, 101.5, 93.1, 73.0,
58.8, 56.3, 18.3, 0.8. Anal. calcd.for C24H32NOSi, Calcd for C, 76.22; H,
8.28; N, 3.71. Found C, 76.22; H : 8.41; N, 3.69. syn : 1H NMR (CDCl3,
400 MHz) 7.31 (m, 10H), 5.78 (dq, J = 6.6 Hz, J = 16 Hz, 1H), 5.32 (ddd,
J = 7.3 Hz, J = 16 Hz, J = 1.6Hz, 1H), 4.01 (dd, J = 7 Hz, J = 9.7 Hz,
1H), 3.88 (d, J = 13.4 Hz, 2H), 3.43 (d, J = 13.4 Hz, 2H), 3.23 (d, J =
9.7 Hz, 1H), 1.70 (dd, J = 6.6 Hz, J = 1.24Hz, 3H), 0.24 (s,9H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 100MHz) 138.2 129.6, 129.6, 129.2, 128.6, 127.4, 99.9, 92.6,
71.1, 58.8, 55.0, 17.8, 0.2.
