(7). In a glove box dIpcBH4 ((2.87 g, 10 mmol) was weighed into a 250 mL
round bottom flask containing a stir bar. (Note: If the borane is
crystalline, then it should be crushed and pulverized with a glass rod
prior to use in order to ensure efficient hydroboration). The flask was
capped with a rubber septum and removed from the glove box and place in
an ice bath. Ether (30 mL) was added to the flask followed by the
allenylboronic ester5 (1.23 g, 10 mmol) added neat via syringe. The
reaction was stirred 2 h in an ice bath during which time the solid
borane dissolved to leave a colorless solution. The ice bath was removed
and the reaction cooled to -78 °C with a dry ice-acetone bath. Aldehyde
56 (1.20 g, 5.4 mmol) was added dropwise. The reaction was stirred 2 h
and then aldehyde 67 (3.16 g, 20 mmol) was added dropwise and the
reaction was allowed to stir an additional hour at -78 °C. The reaction
was allowed to warm to 23 °C over 3 h and then stirred for an additional
24 h. The reaction was cooled in an ice bath and 10 mL of 3M NaOH
solution was added dropwise followed by 4 mL of a 50% H2O2 solution.
(Caution: If the addition of the peroxide is too rapid, then the a
significant exotherm can occur). The reaction was allowed to stir at 23
°C for 4 h at which time it was diluted with 400 mL of CH2Cl2 and 200 mL
of sat. NaHCO3 and 50 mL of sat. NaCl solution. The biphasic mixture was
vigorously stirred for 20 min and then the organic layer was separated
and the aqueous layer washed with CH2Cl2 (3 x 50 mL). The reaction was
dried over Na2SO4 and the solvent removed in vacuo. The residual oil was
purified by column chromatography (gradient elution 10-45% EtOAc in
hexanes) to afford diol 7 (1.74 g) as a colorless oil. An analytical
sample was prepared by preparative HPLC (60:40, EtOAc-exanes). The
absolute configuration and enantiomeric excess were confirmed by analysis
of the bis-Mosher ester: e.e. 94%. (2S, 6R,
4E)-1-[(tert-butyldimethylsilyl)-oxy]-10-para-methoxy-benzyloxy-dec-4-ene-2,6-diol
(7)., yield 73% [α]D 24 = -4.5⁰ (c = 1.05, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.24-7.21 (m, 2H), 6.86-6.83 (m, 2H), 5.64 (dt, J = 7, 15,5 Hz,
1H), 5.53 (dd, J = 6.5, 15.5 Hz, 1H), 4.40 (s, 2H), 4.03 (ddd, app q, J =
6, 6, 6 Hz, 1H), 3.77 (s, 3H), 3.68-3.63 (m, 1H), 3.58 (dd, J = 4, 10 Hz,
1H), 3.45- 3.39 (m, 3H), 2.6 (s, broad -OH, 1H), 2.25-2.18 (m, 2H), 2.10
(s, broad -OH, 1H), 1.65-1.35 (m, 6H), 0.88 (s, 9H), 0.05 (s, 6H); 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.01, 135.88, 130.55, 129.18, 126.99, 113.66,
72.51, 72.45, 71.24, 69.87, 66.51, 55.17, 36.86, 35.80, 29.49, 25.81,
22.06, 18.21, -5.42, -5.45; IR (thin film) 3401, 2930, 2857, 1613, 1514,
1471, 1361, 1249, 1099 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C24H42O5SiNa (M+Na)+
461.2699, found 461.2695 m/z .
